  "caption": "3am: Quinn rolls onto the sore shoulder. Nope. The other side? Also nope. A new mattress didn't help either.\n\nNight shoulder pain is mostly about position. Lying on the sore side compresses irritated tissue, and lying on the good side can let the arm drag forward. The rotator cuff or bursa is often involved.\n\nWhat can help: lie on your good side hugging a pillow, or on your back with the sore arm propped on a pillow, try a little heat before bed, stay off the sore side for now, and keep up daytime strengthening, which works on the cause.\n\nGet it checked if night pain comes with fever, weight loss, constant pain, a cancer history, a big injury or chest symptoms.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
